EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Cradle_and_The_Crescent_MythicPersia_InitiationScripts" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Cradle & The Crescent - Chapter Eight: Mythic Persia initiation scripts"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-07"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Cradle_and_The_Crescent_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's initiation scripts, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t343b6027798f1db1d311c4 ^"Initiation of Solomonic Sihr and the Rank of Mustajib" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tMCInitiationScriptTypeAAAA ^"Initiation Script"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ease Factor" STRING "21"
            ^"Script Bonus" STRING "+18"
            ^"Grants" STRING "Solomonic Sihr and the Rank of Mustajib"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 164
        }
        DESCRIPTION "**Ease Factor**: 21 **Script Bonus**: +18 **Details**: This rite takes place at Alamut during Ramadan (+3). The Initiate is taken to the garden and magically transported to the Magic Realm by his mystagogue (using Solomonic Travel). He finds himself in an insula (see *Realms of Power: Magic*, page 19) of intense paradise, populated with beautiful maidens to cater to his every need. He must quest to find himself a companion spirit through which he will work his magic (+3), and in the process of this quest his magic is bound very closely to a weapon that represents that spirit, imposing the Necessary Condition (brandishing a weapon) onto all of the character’s magic (+9).\n\nWhen he returns to the mundane world with the vision of paradise still filling his head, he is told that the master of Alamut can return him to paradise at any time, and he is promised a place in paradise permanently if he dies in his service. In return he swears a magically-enforced oath to never betray the secrets of the sect, lest he be damned to eternal fire (the Prohibition Flaw, +3).\n\nThe ritual that Opens the Arts of a Gifted Nizari has similar elements to this Initiation, although it does not impose any Flaws."
    }

    #ta41c1857ded763a56cb598 ^"Initiation of Solomonic Storytelling" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tMCInitiationScriptTypeAAAA ^"Initiation Script"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ease Factor" STRING "21"
            ^"Script Bonus" STRING "+15"
            ^"Grants" STRING "Solomonic Storytelling"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 164
        }
        DESCRIPTION "**Ease Factor**: 21 **Script Bonus**: +15 **Details**: The initiate is asked to surrender all contact with the outside world and devote himself to the sect. He must donate all his possessions and land to the Nizaris, and cut off all ties with family and friends. Even his name is changed to a cultic name (+2).\n\nThe initiatory rite takes place at Alamut when Sirius rises (+3); the initiate is taken once more to the paradise insula within the Magic Realm. He must quest on at least three different insulae (thus navigating the Void that separates them), and obtain three objects that resonate with three different emotions (+6).\n\nUpon returning to the mundane world, he must spend a season composing an encoded poem which tells of his journey while appearing to be about an entirely different subject, demonstrating his mastery of the batin (+1).\n\nAfter this second visit to paradise, the mustajib discovers that any use of his magic briefly transports him mentally back there (simulated by the Disorientating Magic Flaw, +3)."
    }

}
